hi there steve kaufman here  today i want to talk about  our language goals and re-evaluating our  language goals i'm going to do that  because i am re-evaluating some of my  goals in this  nine-month you know extreme language  learning project  and i had another i had a few sort of  interactions which again confirmed to me  the need to every so often reevaluate  what we're doing  remember if you enjoy these videos  please subscribe i talk about language  learning sometimes i speak in other  languages  uh and of course if you like the video  give me a like apparently that's good  for me  good for my ratings and all that stuff  uh but  i don't i really don't care uh so  reevaluating my goals first thing that  happened is that i i began to realize  that you know i'm working on three  languages arabic persian and turkish and  really that's too much i can't  concentrate one of my motivations was  that if i left you know when i was doing  three months of one and three months say  three months of arabic three months of  persian three months of turkish by the  time i got back to arabic i had slipped  too much so i said well i kind of it's  like having three pots on the burner if  i kind of keep them all simmering  then i won't fall too far behind in any  one of them  but i'm finding that you know the  challenge of arabic and persian the  challenge of learning to read in a  different writing system  but it's the same writing system arabic  and persian slightly different  now that's sufficient there's a lot of  work to be done there  and that the turkish actually is a lot  easier the language itself is difficult  different at any rate  but it's written in the latin alphabet  so it's kind of easier in a way so that  if i go back to turkish in nine months i  don't think i'll lose that much i think  i can get back to it pretty quickly i am  motivated to do turkish but i'm also  motivated to achieve more progress in  arabic and persian so i have to make a  choice so i've decided  i'm going to focus on arabic and persian  same writing system get better and  better at reading  that  script which will in turn make me a  better reader make it easier for me to  acquire vocabulary so i have decided to  focus on those two  languages i mentioned that i am in touch  with uh people in in persian that are  creating stories about themselves  uh we've now got 10 in a course at link  called the iranians  uh unfortunately not unfortunately but  it's mostly women i'd like to have more  male voices there just to have a better  balance but there are very interesting  short descriptions of ordinary people  ordinary iranians you know  iran kind of is getting pretty bad press  these days but it's important to realize  that those are individual people who  live there who aren't very different in  terms of their aspirations and what they  want to do and how they interact with  their family members and so forth in  most cases not very different from  the way people in other countries are so  the iranians as a course enables me to  learn about the language and learn about  people  and i'm also continuing to you know use  news podcasts similarly in  uh arabic and i'm beginning to feel as  i'm understanding more and more of it  more and more of the words are known to  me more and more when i listen i  understand  uh which is you know a a great feeling  that feeling that you're starting to  make some  some significant you know uh uh  improvement and so if i leave turkish  and put it aside i don't think that's  gonna be a problem so i'm focusing  completely focusing now on arabic and  persian so that's where i stand on  reevaluating my objectives i was also  i noticed that uh luca lamporiella who  is an excellent lamborghini excellent  polyglot recently did a video where he  says that he has decided to stop his  japanese efforts for now he said it was  a failure i don't think it's a failure  i'm sure he speaks japanese quite well  but not as well as he would like and so  he has decided for whatever reason to  set that aside and do something else and  i'm sure that if something were to come  along that would very much motivate him  then he would jump back into his  japanese studies and he would do very  well because he has he is a very  experienced language learner  i was talking to someone from japan  yesterday uh a video that you will see  here shortly  and i was exp and i was asked what my  advice to  sort of language learners in japan was  and i sort of said you know  that the language learning is such a  rewarding activity but we have to do it  in a way that's enjoyable because that  way we stay with it and if we stay with  it we will  improve and she said yeah but  unfortunately in japan people have to  pass tests so that becomes their focus  and i said yeah but if they really  evaluate their objectives they will  realize that in order to do well on  those exams you have to enjoy the  process so you have to find a way to  enjoy it and so  doing you know trying to learn from  lists of words or doing all these drills  and exercises or mock tests moctoic  tests etc actually is not getting you  closer to your objective if you really  looked at what your objective was i mean  you want to improve in the language if  you have a toeic score and then  maybe you can somehow ace the test  without knowing the language which i  doubt  then if you are in working for a company  where you have to go and interact with  people from foreign countries you won't  do very well so ultimately the real goal  is to get you know to improve your level  in the language if you improve your  level in the language then you will do  well on the tests and then you'll be  effective using the language and so  really the goal should be  as i've often said with language  instruction as well how do we make it  enjoyable how do we make it enjoyable  because if it is enjoyable people will  stay with it now  my turkish was enjoyable but i had too  much on my plate it's like if you go to  a  restaurant and you want to try  everything on the menu but you can't eat  everything on the menu so you have to  make a choice so  that's why  right now i have decided that my 90 day  not  nine months rather challenge extreme  language learning where i was going to  do three languages  i have finally decided i mean i may  occasionally look at turkish  just so it doesn't get too far away from  me but i'm gonna focus my energies on  arabic and persian so i have reevaluated  my objectives and i'm focusing in on two  languages which is still a tall order  and i hope to be building up our library  at link as i go so i  anyway you'll see we'll have more and  more material there for  arabic and persian  okay that's what i wanted to say and if  you want to uh take my uh  get uh subscribe to my 10 email course  on how to learn languages uh make sure  you click through on the link that's  here on the screen thank you bye for now

